{"instruction":"Answer the accounting question.","input":"What is depreciation?","output":"Depreciation is the accounting method used to allocate the cost of a tangible asset over its useful life."}
{"instruction":"Answer the accounting question.","input":"What is amortization?","output":"Amortization is the process of gradually writing off the cost of an intangible asset over its useful life."}
{"instruction":"Answer the accounting question.","input":"What is goodwill?","output":"Goodwill is an intangible asset that arises when a company acquires another company for more than the fair value of its net identifiable assets."}
{"instruction":"Answer the accounting question.","input":"What is straight-line depreciation?","output":"Straight-line depreciation allocates an equal depreciation expense each year over an asset’s useful life."}

